@startuml Load Sign-off and Declarations

title Signing off a vehicle's load and filing its declarations
caption Target design. Decisions P6, X3, X6, X5, D4, D12, D20, X1, O32. ADRs 0004, 0005, 0006, 0003, 0002.

autonumber

actor Dispatcher as disp
actor Administrator as admin
actor "Ground Officer" as go
actor "Receiver\n(Ukraine)" as rcv
participant "Freedom API" as api
database "Freedom database" as db
queue "Customs queues" as q
participant "Customs Worker" as cw
participant "EU Customs\nTrader Portal" as eu
participant "HMRC (GVMS)" as hmrc
participant "French customs (ELO)" as elo
participant "Ukraine\nhumanitarian aid system" as ua

== Allocate boxes and sign off the load ==
disp -> api : allocate attested boxes to the vehicle
disp -> api : POST /manifests/{id}/propose
admin -> api : POST /manifests/{id}/approve
api -> db : manifest Approved (sign-off only)
note right of api
  Approval no longer files or enqueues anything.
  Declarations are prepared after sign-off; filing is a separate act.
end note

== Each declaration is per vehicle ==
disp -> api : mark declaration Ready to file
api -> db : store a snapshot of the load

== ENS (always manual) ==
disp -> api : GET ENS filing sheet
api --> disp : everything except the consignee address\n(organisation and region only)
disp -> eu : file the ENS
go -> eu : enter the consignee address (O32)
note right of go
  Freedom never shows the address to the Dispatcher.
end note
eu --> disp : MRN
disp -> api : record ENS MRN (write-once)
api -> db : ENS Accepted

== ELO (needs the ENS MRN first) ==
alt ELO mode = manual (default)
  disp -> elo : request the envelope by hand
  elo --> disp : envelope reference
  disp -> api : record ELO reference
  api -> db : ELO Filed
else ELO mode = automatic
  disp -> api : file ELO
  api -> db : refuse unless ENS Accepted
  api -> q : enqueue envelope request
  api -> db : ELO Filed (on enqueue)
  q -> cw : envelope request
  cw -> elo : create envelope
  elo --> cw : file number + barcode
  cw -> cw : store in blob storage
end

== GMR ==
alt GMR mode = manual (default)
  disp -> hmrc : create GMR in the portal
  hmrc --> disp : GMR id
  disp -> api : record GMR reference
else GMR mode = automatic
  disp -> api : file GMR
  api -> q : enqueue GMR submission
  q -> cw : submission
  cw -> hmrc : create GMR
end

== Ukrainian goods list (one per Receiver per vehicle) ==
disp -> api : prepare goods list (rolled up from the boxes)
api --> disp : goods list (UKTZED codes, quantities, weights, values)
disp -> rcv : send goods list
rcv -> ua : file the goods list (only a registered recipient can)
ua --> rcv : unique code
rcv --> disp : unique code
disp -> api : record goods-list reference
api -> db : goods list Filed

note over disp, api
  Refusals keep only a bounded reason code, never the authority's free text.
  The Dispatcher is warned a week before a code or declaration expires (D34).
end note

@enduml
